{
  "id": "27842_mazeawaseru",
  "headword": "{混|ま}ぜ{合|あ}わせる",
  "reading": "まぜあわせる",
  "romaji": "mazeawaseru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to mix together; to blend; to combine",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to mix together; to blend; to combine",
      "explanation": "To stir or fold two or more substances together so they form a single uniform mixture. The {合|あ}わせる element stresses bringing the parts together into one."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27842_mazeawaseru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{材料|ざいりょう}を{混|ま}ぜ{合|あ}わせる。",
      "english": "Mix the ingredients together.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27842_mazeawaseru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{二|ふた}つの{色|いろ}の{絵|え}の{具|ぐ}を{混|ま}ぜ{合|あ}わせた。",
      "english": "I blended two colors of paint together.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27842_mazeawaseru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{卵|たまご}と{砂糖|さとう}をよく{混|ま}ぜ{合|あ}わせてから、{小麦粉|こむぎこ}を{加|くわ}える。",
      "english": "Blend the eggs and sugar well, then add the flour.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Compound of {混|ま}ぜる (to mix) + {合|あ}わせる (to put together). Common in cooking and craft instructions for combining multiple ingredients into one.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {材料|ざいりょう}を{混|ま}ぜ{合|あ}わせる: to combine the ingredients\n- よく{混|ま}ぜ{合|あ}わせる: to mix thoroughly\n- {均一|きんいつ}に{混|ま}ぜ{合|あ}わせる: to blend evenly\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {混|ま}ぜる: to mix — simpler; {混|ま}ぜ{合|あ}わせる emphasizes blending several things into one uniform whole",
